>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1780286077250552083":{"a":"<p>That&#x27;s a super important one to understand. A double hamburger (120g beef) is about 20g of protein. I&#x27;ve noticed many people think that the hamburger would be 120g of protein and they starve themselves while eating mountains of carbs. If you feel hungry constantly that&#x27;s a hint. <a href=\"https://x.com/KingBeauregard/status/1780253423889191035\">Tweet by @KingBeauregard</a></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/KingBeauregard/status/1780253423889191035\">https://x.com/KingBeauregard/status/1780253423889191035</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1780286077250552083</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1780286077250552083\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-04-16T17:24:11Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1780302733980877245":{"a":"<p>I think 4½ hours is too much Joe Rogan. 😜 <a href=\"https://x.com/Anyextee/status/1780296899595247984\">Tweet by @Anyextee</a></p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\" data-conversation=\"none\" data-dnt=\"true\"><a href=\"https://x.com/Anyextee/status/1780296899595247984\">https://x.com/Anyextee/status/1780296899595247984</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1780302733980877245</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1780302733980877245\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-04-16T18:30:22Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>thread</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>thread_count</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>conversation</dt><dd>1780302733980877245</dd>\n</dl>"},"1780303477001924619":{"a":"<p>I seem to have a guard bee at my usual sitting spot. We&#x27;ve come to an agreement. I&#x27;m going to eat my tacos and if anything with wings comes near them fair game. 😂 t.co</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1780303477001924619\">https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1780303477001924619</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1780303477001924619</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1780303477001924619\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-04-16T18:33:20Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1780310661337080216":{"a":"<p>@Anyextee @Graham__Hancock @FlintDibble @joerogan My take on @FlintDibble is that he&#x27;s not as open to ideas as his excellent speaking voice conveys. I don&#x27;t take issue with what he says, though. He&#x27;s right in everything he says, most likely. The question perhaps is what was under the ice that no longer exists? t.co</p>\n\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1780296899595247984\">https://x.com/i/status/1780296899595247984</a></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/Anyextee/status/1780296899595247984\">https://x.com/Anyextee/status/1780296899595247984</a></blockquote>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1780310661337080216\">https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1780310661337080216</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1780310661337080216</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1780310661337080216\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-04-16T19:01:52Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>1</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1780311210795077698":{"a":"<p>@Anyextee @Graham__Hancock @FlintDibble @joerogan He says metallurgy didn&#x27;t exist because there&#x27;s no ice for evidence for it. That assumes advanced technology needs to burn coal to make steel, for example.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1780310661337080216\">https://x.com/i/status/1780310661337080216</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1780311210795077698</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1780311210795077698\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-04-16T19:04:03Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1780312408940028035":{"a":"<p>@Anyextee @Graham__Hancock @FlintDibble @joerogan The Earth is covered in soil. Where did that soil come from and when? What happens if you look closely at places where soil doesn&#x27;t exist. For example, Iceland. Look at the geometry of the geothermal vent network.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1780311210795077698\">https://x.com/i/status/1780311210795077698</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1780312408940028035</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1780312408940028035\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-04-16T19:08:49Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1780313192163356802":{"a":"<p>@Anyextee @Graham__Hancock @FlintDibble @joerogan Why is the entire planet covered in structures that are precisely 0.42 nautical miles apart? Why are those structures identical in geometry; even though they are covered in local artwork.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/i/status/1780312408940028035\">https://x.com/i/status/1780312408940028035</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1780313192163356802</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1780313192163356802\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-04-16T19:11:56Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>reply</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd